# Code owners for release and supply-chain surfaces.
#
# Changes to these paths alter what gets built, published, or trusted: CI
# workflows and guardrail scripts, dependency manifests and lockfiles (Cargo,
# npm, Scarb, Swift, Gradle, pub),
# license/advisory policy, release playbooks, git hooks, and the security
# policy. They need a designated reviewer rather than any available approver.
# Owners: the repository admins. Extend the list as the team grows; ownership
# here does not replace the
# branch-protection rules configured in the repository settings.

